<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Xuanzong of Jin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1163–1224</span> · Also known as Wanyan Xun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Xuanzong of Jin (1163–1224), personal name Wanyan Xun, was emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a> from 1213 to 1224. Placed on the throne after a coup killed his predecessor during the Mongol invasion, he bought a truce from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> in 1214 with tribute and a princess, then moved the court south from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhongdu">Zhongdu</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a>, which led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> to resume the war. He also fought costly wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and Western Xia.</p></div>
